WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.803
-Our next guests are sisters
and best-selling authors

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.405
whose new book, "The World
Record Book of Racist Stories,"

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:07.907
is on sale now.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.710
Please welcome back to the show
Amber Ruffin and Lacey Lamar!

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.678
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:21.387 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:30.096 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:33.299
-Welcome back, you guys!
-Yay! Hi!

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.668
-Before we get started, Amber,

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.404
did you make Lacey
dress like you?

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:39.739
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.107
-Uh-huh.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.710
-Did you make anybody else
dress like you?

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.511
-Mnh-mnh.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:47.180
-Are you lying?

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.081
-Mnh-mnh.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.484
-Tom, is she lying?

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.952
-She's lying, Seth.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.854
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.556
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.556 --> 00:00:59.325
-He does look great.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.861
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.563
-Looks beautiful.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.665
-I'd like you to know
Amber came in this morning

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.499
and pitched that idea,
and I said, "I mean,

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:08.701
is Tom okay with it?"

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.203
And she was like,
"Yeah, yeah, yeah."

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:13.005
-Tom came up to me.

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.407
[ Laughter ]
-Alright.

00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:17.776
So, now, last time
you were here, Lacey,

00:01:17.776 --> 00:01:20.046
this was very in line
with your previous appearance

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.081
where Amber made you dress
and have the --

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.949
Were you expecting this
when you came?

00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:26.519
-No. She stole my look.
-She stole your look both times.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.554
Alright, so, the first book,
which is a best-seller --

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:31.324
congratulations --
was based on --

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.759
[ Cheers and applause ]
Absolutely.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.961
These were based on stories --
You live in Omaha, Nebraska.

00:01:35.961 --> 00:01:38.598
Obviously your sister
lives in New York City.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:42.501
They were stories you would tell
her that she could not believe.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:45.171
Was this -- What made you

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.673
then come to this idea
of a second book?

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:50.409
-Because we had too many stories
to fit into the first book.

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:53.379
-Yeah.
-And I'm still living there,

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.682
and so these things are
constantly happening to me.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.817
So Amber's like, "We should
probably write a second book."

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.285
And I'm like,
"It's writing itself."

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.589
-And these are -- these are --
And I think there's a real --

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.224
I mean, it's a weird way
to describe this book,

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:07.727
but it is an education
that's in the form of a gift.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.729
You're both very funny.
You're both very honest.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.798
You both seem like
very loving people,

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.766
and yet you,
in very clear-eyed ways,

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.902
describe these racist things
that happen to you both.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.271
And I think it's helpful
for people like myself

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.906
to read them and be like,
"Oh, my God. I knew it was bad.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.676
I did not quite understand
the depths of this."

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.679
-Yeah, people don't --
That's part of the reason

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:30.350
why we wrote the first book,
is because of the sheer volume

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.117
of these things.

00:02:32.117 --> 00:02:36.856
It's one tiny lady's
lifetime of garbage,

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:40.493
and it's so funny
because she's not a --

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.929
she's not special in any way.
-What?

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.998
-No, I'm just kidding! I'm just
kidding! I'm just kidding!

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:50.035
She's not, like, angry
or mean or bad in any way.

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:52.872
She's just this cute
little happy guy,

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:56.042
and that all happens to her.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.411
-And these stories, you have to
read them to believe them.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:02.215
Are there any good examples of
exactly what we're dealing with?

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.682
-Oh, yes.

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:05.285
So, not too long ago,

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.086
right before the second book
was finished,

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.420
I went to the car dealership.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.289
I was going to
purchase a new car.

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:12.191
And I'm looking at this car,
and I say, "You know what?

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:14.160
If I pay cash on this,
can you do any better?"

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.494
And they're like,
"Absolutely not.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:16.995
That's not a thing.
We don't do that."

00:03:16.995 --> 00:03:18.164
I said, "Okay."

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.867
I left, immediately
called a family friend --

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:23.236
-Because she knows
damn well they do that.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:26.105
Everyone knows they do that.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.540
-White gentleman.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.241
He's like, "I live for this.
I'm on my way."

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:31.510
He goes there, looks --
I mean, this is in minutes.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.479
Same car. Sa--

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.682
He offers cash,
same amount of money,

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.350
and they said,
"Oh, we'll take $4,000 off."

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.885
-Really?! They gave a $4,000 --

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:41.754
-Both: $4,000!

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:45.257
-And they at no point could
smell that this was some...

00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:47.393
-No, I love it because the --
the guy calls me and goes,

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.561
"You know what? You need to come
back and look at this car

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:51.597
because someone's
looking at it."

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:54.100
-So then she calls them back.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.103
She says, "I sent
my white friend in there,

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.105
and you gave him $4,000 off."

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:01.373
And they said,
"Okay, okay. Fine.

00:04:01.373 --> 00:04:03.710
You can have $1,000 off."

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.211
-Swear to God.
-Can you believe it?!

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.112
-I only got $1,000 off.
-That's amazing.

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:09.749
-She didn't buy --
-I didn't buy the car.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.784
-So, you said you wrote
this last book

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.786
at your parents' house
while drinking margaritas.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.555
Was that your process
for the second book?

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.956
-Yeah, pretty much.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.524
-Okay, good, yeah.
You also admitted

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.760
that your mother would not enjoy
reading the first book.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.862
Did she change her tune
on the second?

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.697
-We're still grounded
from the last book.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.164
-Yeah.
-I shouldn't even be here.

00:04:26.164 --> 00:04:27.633
-But you got her to agree

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.869
to participate and tell
some of her own stories.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.905
-We're bigger and stronger
than she is, Seth.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:36.609
-Tiny little lady.
-So you just bullied her into --

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:39.178
-"When was the last time
you felt like this?!"

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:42.248
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:45.117
-I mean, do you think --
I mean, she must be proud

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:47.186
of the fact that this is a book
that is circulating

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.155
and people are reading
and people are enjoying.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.990
-No, she is. She's very proud.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.592
She just explicitly said...

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:55.395
-Both: "Do not..."
-"...put me in the book."

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.730
-"...put me in the book."
-And then we did.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.266
And then we said --
That was the first book.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.901
That was flagrant.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.369
But then the second book,
we said,

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:07.873
"We will tell your stories the
way you want them to be told.

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:11.177
And we won't put in
a lot of the stories

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:15.714
where, you know, you, um --
uh, defend your children."

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.016
How about that?
Let's say it like that.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.251
-Well, right. Because she does
come off very heroically

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:21.320
as someone who defends
and stands up for her kids.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.056
You got other people in your
family, other people in your --

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:25.991
your circle of friends

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:28.561
to commit their stories to you
and tell you stories.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:31.130
Were most people
sort of eager to do that

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.965
or were most people hesitant?

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:34.734
-I think a lot of people
were eager.

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:37.737
Our whole family, our brothers,
our sisters, everybody was fine.

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:39.372
And then people
in the community were --

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.006
There are a lot of people
that were like,

00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:42.341
"Ooh, I have a story."

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:45.178
I'm like, "Of course you do.
You're my neighbor."

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:47.113
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:49.549
-I have a lot more to ask
you guys, especially about

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:53.018
a very special person
that you guys got to meet.

00:05:53.018 --> 00:05:54.353
We'll be right back with more

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:56.589
from Amber Ruffin
and Lacey Lamar.

